# bar_lure_stealth_arrows (kenshi-h2v.27.2 check): bar_lure's ground with the Wanderer sneaking in front of three Hub citizens (neutral, the town's
# faction), who notice him. One arrow.mesh per DETECTED_BY entry floats on the line to each: yellow while a citizen is noticing (record state 2), red
# once it is noticed (state 1); sneaking off clears them. Two citizens face him head-on (yaw 2.98 and 3.315), the third sees him at the edge of its
# cone (yaw 1.74, about 63 degrees off its forward): its notice meter fills slower, so a moment of one yellow and two red arrows exists. The
# stealth skill is pinned at 95 (stats=stealth:95) so the fill takes seconds, long enough to catch and to outlast the client's load. They are not
# hostile, the town is not at war with the player (the user's "flooded with red arrows but they're not enemies" case).
# Only the player is ever ordered (SCENARIO_IMPORT.md "Rule").
